{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Fix pushed as Gerrit change 1486 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1486), **Verified +1** on patch set 1 (GH Actions run 31171494815, all 4 pytest cells green: ubuntu py3.11/3.12/3.13 + macos py3.13). That green run is the proof of AC #1 — the previously-skipped 38 tests now actually EXECUTE in the gate.\n\nOption chosen: add `--extra reviewbot --extra ui` to the EXISTING pytest lane install in _build-and-test.yml (the matrix job), not a dedicated lane and not folding reviewbot into `dev`.\n- a dedicated lane would double the longest job in the gate (the default suite is already 15m+ on macOS and holds a scarce runner slot, ticket f3d4) for a 38-test surface;\n- folding into `dev` would defeat the lean-core invariant _optionality.yml polices and push fastapi onto every contributor;\n- appending an extra to an existing lane is exactly what test.yml:101 already does for `agents`.\nCost is a handful of small pure-python wheels (fastapi, jinja2, and uvicorn's uvloop/watchfiles/websockets stack). No test needs network or AWS credentials: boto3 is only touched on the best-effort CloudWatch publish in voter.py, which none of these tests exercise, and the suite's own socket guard still holds.\n\nRegression guard (AC #3), designed to detect tests NOT RUNNING rather than an extra merely being named in a workflow file: `REBAR_REQUIRE_EXTRAS=1` is set on both pytest steps, and tests/_extra_guard.py swaps `pytest.importorskip` for a variant that RAISES instead of skipping. A lost extra then reddens the build by module name — collection error for a module-scope call, test error for a function-scope one — with a message pointing at the install step. Deliberately scoped: skips keyed on a missing binary or version floor (ssh-keygen >= 8.9, Node for e2e) are `skipif`, not `importorskip`, and stay skippable.\n\nAC #2 (deliberate break -> CI red) proven locally in the faithful form: with fastapi uninstalled, tests/unit/test_review_bot_token_redaction.py reports `4 skipped` today and `4 failed` with the guard armed; tests/unit/test_opcert_service_app.py goes from a whole-module skip to a collection ERROR. Full local suite with the guard armed: 10969 passed, 26 skipped — and every remaining skip is skipif-based (playwright/Node, ssh-keygen, GNU coreutils, the deliberate llm-optionality degradation cases). Zero importorskip skips remain.\n\nUnrelated pre-existing local failure seen while verifying: tests/unit/metrics/test_jscpd_dup_heldout.py::test_live_clone (assert 0 >= 1) fails identically on untouched origin/main — already being fixed on Gerrit change 1487 (ticket 4bf4)."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786101618113164001,"uuid":"a5e76671-2654-4dba-8251-0dd5ac1d61f9"}